            "review_text": "pablomasters\nDallas, Texas9 contributions\n0\nClean and local\nAug 2017 • Couples\nMe and my wife visited this restaurant last week at night, when the lighting and the ambience gave it a more appealing touch compared to how I'm sure it would look during the day and were pleased to discover that, for cheap, the quality of the soup and the fish we had was exquisite and this accompanied by an amicable attitude coming from the waitress, we didn't have to wait over 10 minutes and the food was hot and tasted, and smelled fresh. My wife spent some time after the meal to discover the pottery the owner has at the back, she was entertained. We had a good time. Traditional taste for a few dollars (we had 2 meals for less than $25).\n\nFavor this kind of resto over tourism focused ones that collect for the decoration and the name.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten August 22, 2017",
